msgid "PHP2Shell: PHP version"
msgstr ""

msgid "PHP2Shell check"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Read from the PHP process that serves this site. Nothing is sent anywhere."
msgstr ""

msgid "You have marked the PHP2Shell fixes as confirmed by your host"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"PHP reports version %s, which is lower than the first fixed releases, but "
"you told this plugin that your host confirmed the fixes. This plugin cannot "
"verify that."
msgstr ""

msgid "Your PHP version includes the PHP2Shell fixes"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"PHP reports version %1$s, which is equal to or newer than %2$s, the first "
"release of the %3$s branch with the fixes for CVE-2026-109618 and "
"CVE-2026-109619. This is the version of the process that is serving this "
"page."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"PHP reports version %1$s. The %2$s branch is newer than the ones listed in "
"the PHP advisory (8.2 to 8.5) and includes their fixes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Your PHP version is lower than the one that fixes PHP2Shell"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"PHP reports version %1$s, which is lower than %2$s, the first release of the"
" %3$s branch with the fixes for CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"That does not prove your site is exposed. Distributions such as Debian or "
"Ubuntu ship the fix without changing the version number PHP reports, and "
"this plugin cannot tell the difference from inside WordPress. Ask your host."
msgstr ""

msgid "Your PHP branch has no official PHP2Shell fix"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"PHP reports version %s. The PHP project has not released official versions "
"with the fixes for PHP 8.1 and older (it only published minimal source "
"patches), so your protection depends on your host applying a backported fix."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Ask your host whether they have applied it, or move your site to a supported"
" PHP version."
msgstr ""

msgid "You are running a pre-release PHP build"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"PHP reports version %s, a pre-release build. Pre-release builds are not "
"meant for production sites."
msgstr ""

