msgid ""
"This site runs PHP as an Apache module (mod_php). PHP considers it the most "
"exposed setup, because the attack can succeed before any application code "
"runs."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The file %s sets session.upload_progress.enabled. PHP warns that .user.ini "
"does not take effect in time for this mitigation, so do not count it as "
"applied: set it in php.ini or in the PHP-FPM pool."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The setting session.upload_progress.enabled is on, which is the PHP default."
" Turning it off in php.ini or in the PHP-FPM pool is an extra mitigation "
"recommended by PHP, and the only one it lists for CVE-2026-115560, a third "
"flaw that has no fixed release yet. It does not replace updating PHP, and on"
" shared hosting only your host can apply it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Branch 8.2 stopped receiving security fixes on 31 December 2026."
msgstr ""

msgid "Branch 8.2 stops receiving security fixes on 31 December 2026."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hello, have you applied the PHP patches for CVE-2026-109618 and "
"CVE-2026-109619 (PHP 8.2.35, 8.3.36, 8.4.27, 8.5.12 or the equivalent "
"backported fix) on the servers where my site runs? My site currently reports"
" PHP %1$s running as %2$s. Can you confirm which package version is "
"installed and that the PHP processes were restarted after the update?"
